WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.749
Good morning, it's Monday, November 23.

00:00:02.819 --> 00:00:10.221
This is Signal in the AI Fog, your daily briefing on enterprise AI in production, written and read by AI.

00:00:10.291 --> 00:00:20.089
Today: Anthropic shares fall after record debut, Gemini 3.6 Flash shutdown set for January, and Walmart's agent profiles still unconfirmed.

00:00:20.159 --> 00:00:22.133
First, the story of the day.

00:00:22.203 --> 00:00:30.380
Anthropic shares fell 8.5 percent on Friday, November twentieth, their first full day of trading, according to CNBC.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:42.080
The stock had opened at 111 dollars 50 on Thursday after the company raised 81.3 billion dollars, the largest IPO of all time, then closed that day at 97 dollars 17.

00:00:42.151 --> 00:00:44.195
The IPO price was 83 dollars.

00:00:44.266 --> 00:00:52.442
Yahoo Finance reports that the implied valuation briefly approached two trillion dollars during the opening session.

00:00:52.512 --> 00:00:57.517
Friday's drop came as tech stocks slid, with Nvidia and AMD also lower.

00:00:57.587 --> 00:01:01.535
CNN reports the Nasdaq wiped out its gains for the year.

00:01:01.605 --> 00:01:08.795
Reuters, cited by Yahoo Finance, describes Anthropic as the first publicly traded frontier AI company.

00:01:08.865 --> 00:01:18.240
CNBC also quotes the US Treasury Secretary saying the company has been cooperative in pre-testing its models with the administration.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:26.546
The read here: a first public frontier vendor now has a share price that moves with AI sentiment, not with your usage.

00:01:26.611 --> 00:01:32.227
That price tells you nothing about model quality, availability or your contract terms.

00:01:32.293 --> 00:01:39.215
What it adds is a quarterly disclosure rhythm, and a vendor under market pressure on spending and margins.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.872
That could, but need not, show up in pricing or quotas.

00:01:42.937 --> 00:01:45.288
It is worth watching, not acting on.

00:01:45.353 --> 00:01:55.671
A swing from a premium of about thirty-four percent at the open to a fall below the first-day close in two sessions is a reminder of how noisy this signal is.

00:01:55.737 --> 00:01:58.937
For a platform team, the discipline is unchanged.

00:01:59.002 --> 00:02:02.267
Keep a second vendor routable through the gateway.

00:02:02.332 --> 00:02:03.377
Time a failover.

00:02:03.442 --> 00:02:10.430
Base routing decisions on your own evaluations and your own cost per task, not on headlines or on a ticker.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:11.984
Next, Platform.

00:02:12.048 --> 00:02:20.126
Google's documentation lists Gemini 3.6 Flash on its Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform with a date of November nineteenth, 2026.

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:26.105
Existing active projects keep access until permanent shutdown on January twenty-eighth, 2027.

00:02:26.169 --> 00:02:30.367
The model had been released on that platform on July twenty-first.

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:43.470
Google says retirement dates apply to support on that platform, that models may remain reachable through the Gemini API, and that its policy gives at least forty-five days to migrate once a date is posted.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:52.231
Why it matters: the shutdown that counts for existing projects is January twenty-eighth, 2027, not this week.

00:02:52.306 --> 00:03:04.645
Use the time to check that no production route, fallback or batch job still depends on the model, and that any replacement you choose has passed your evaluation set.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:09.955
A new model can also change token usage per task, so look at cost too.

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:15.788
The next calendar item, Gemini 2.5 rerouting on December first, is days away.

00:03:15.863 --> 00:03:20.200
Keep these dates as data in your gateway, not in an inbox.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.270
Next, Retail and agents.

00:03:22.331 --> 00:03:33.170
Walmart announced on October twenty-first that Agent Profiles would let customers authorise individual shopping agents, track their purchases separately and set spending limits.

00:03:33.231 --> 00:03:37.824
Its chief executive has said the launch would come over the next few weeks.

00:03:37.885 --> 00:03:48.051
Yahoo Finance still describes Walmart as preparing to launch them, and notes that United Airlines is restricting unauthorised third-party agents from booking flights.

00:03:48.112 --> 00:03:51.970
The sources reviewed do not confirm that the profiles are live.

00:03:52.570 --> 00:04:00.531
The bigger picture: the expected date has slipped past without confirmation, so treat the launch as pending, not delivered.

00:04:00.595 --> 00:04:08.167
The design is the useful part for any retailer: an identity per agent, a separate purchase history and spending caps.

00:04:08.232 --> 00:04:14.186
Add the airline's opposite stance, blocking, and you have the two ends of the posture range.

00:04:14.251 --> 00:04:26.030
Decide where you stand, and specify how an agent identifies itself, what limits apply, and how an order is logged and reversed, before outside agents start arriving at your checkout.

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:28.114
The number of the day.

00:04:28.182 --> 00:04:29.599
81.3 billion dollars.

00:04:29.666 --> 00:04:34.929
That is what Anthropic raised in its IPO, the largest ever, according to CNBC.

00:04:34.996 --> 00:04:38.842
Even so, the shares fell 8.5 percent on their second day.

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:45.319
Capital raised does not settle market confidence, and it does not change your vendor risk plan.

00:04:45.387 --> 00:04:46.331
What to watch.

00:04:46.399 --> 00:04:54.833
This week: Anthropic's shares, to see whether the market slide continues, and what the first weeks of public reporting bring.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:58.611
Prices, quotas and regions for OVHcloud's new products.

00:04:58.678 --> 00:05:02.187
Confirmation that Walmart's Agent Profiles are live.

00:05:02.254 --> 00:05:14.601
Then Carbon's introductory price ends November thirtieth, Gemini 2.5 requests reroute December first, AI Act marking starts December second, and EuroHPC's Lot 2 closes December third.

00:05:14.669 --> 00:05:16.625
And a question for your team.

00:05:16.693 --> 00:05:26.948
Could your gateway shift traffic away from your main model vendor within an hour, and when did you last test that failover with your own evaluation set?

00:05:27.016 --> 00:05:28.365
That's it for today.

00:05:28.433 --> 00:05:31.064
Sources are in the episode description.

00:05:31.131 --> 00:05:33.156
This was Signal in the AI Fog.

00:05:33.223 --> 00:05:34.370
See you tomorrow.
